CONVERSATION 2: FSH of 14, everything already spent on a cycle, ends with a resource and no link

Lead: FSH 14 at 39. we just spent everything we had on a round that didn't work and I don't think we can do another for at least a year. is there any point me even asking you anything

Sonia: There's always a point in asking. I'm not going to tell you what your number means though, because it's one marker, on one day, in a cycle that had a lot else going on, and I can't see any of that from here.

Lead: so what would you even do about it

Sonia: If you were working with me I'd want the year you've just had, not the number. A failed round takes a physical toll that rarely gets accounted for before the next one.

But I want to be honest with you rather than pitch at you. You've just told me the money is gone for a year. Coaching with me is paid, and I'm not going to try and talk you around that.

Lead: I appreciate that. everyone else has tried to sell me something this month.

Sonia: You've had enough of that.

Here's what I'd actually say: a year isn't dead time. It's the longest run-up you'll get, and what happens in it tends to matter more than people expect.

Lead: what should I be doing in it?

Sonia: Watch my masterclass first. It covers what's worth attending to in the months before a cycle, and it costs you nothing but an hour.

